Analysis Report – ZFLTC11N Policy Extraction Issue

Policy Number Analyzed: 5140405
Job/Program Name: ZFLTC11N
Date: June 26, 2025


---

Overview:

An analysis was conducted on the ZFLTC11N job to determine why policy number 5140405 was not appearing in the extract. After reviewing the job logic, it was found that a date-based condition was responsible for excluding this policy.


---

Technical Condition Identified:

IF (WPHST-CHANGE-DATE <= OFFSET-DATE)
    SET PAST-DATE TO TRUE  -- Policy will be ignored

WPHST-CHANGE-DATE: 20200927

OFFSET-DATE (Run Date - 2 weeks): 20250317

Run Date: 20250331


The above logic ensures that only policies with change dates within 2 weeks of the Run Date are included in the extract. Since policy 5140405 has a change date older than the offset date, it was ignored by the job.


---

Resolution Implemented:

For policy 5140405, the condition was bypassed specifically, allowing it to be successfully populated in the extract.


---

Performance Impact & Recommendation:

When the filtering condition was removed globally for all policies, the job behavior changed drastically:

Normal Execution:

Runtime: 1 to 1.5 hours

Output File Size: < 200 MB


Without Filtering Condition (All Policies):

Runtime: Exceeded 4 hours

Output File Size: > 14 GB



Due to this significant degradation in performance, the filtering condition cannot be removed for all policies. Doing so impacts processing time, system performance, and output manageability. Therefore, this condition must remain in place, and any exceptions should be handled on a case-by-case basis.


---

Conclusion:

The filtering condition based on the policy change date is crucial for maintaining optimal job performance. While exceptions can be made for specific policies where justified, removing the condition entirely is not feasible due to the resulting system load and data volume. Future enhancements should focus on improving flexibility while preserving performance.
